From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:33:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: form controls, URL properties, attribute nodes,
 current style, tables, location parts, and the HTML dialogs

Text ranges (createTextRange) of input, textarea and button; the status attribute of input/textarea/button,
input indeterminate, textarea select(); meta httpEquiv/content/name setters; form and select item() by name
or id and tags(); img/anchor fileSize, dates, mimeType, protocol, protocolLong, nameProp and href from the file
or URL behind them (the protocol name is read from the registry only in its "URL:" form); anchor Methods;
frame allowTransparency, margins that take numbers, IHTMLFrameBase2 over IDispatch; object width/height from
any variant; location protocol/host/hostname/port/pathname/search setters (navigate with one part replaced,
through IUriBuilder) and reload of a frame; comment text/atomic; attribute node children as the text of the
value (child list, first/last, has, insert/replace/remove/append edit the value) and cloneNode; current
style clipBottom, getAttribute, blockDirection, zoom, isBlock, hasLayout (display/position based),
msInterpolationMode (set/removeAttribute refuse: it is a computed style); style element readyState,
onreadystatechange, disabled; table cells, moveRow, paging calls (one page without data binding),
dataPageSize, readyState and cellSpacing from any variant; style clip-bottom.

htmldlg.c: ShowHTMLDialog, ShowHTMLDialogEx, ShowModelessHTMLDialog, RunHTMLApplication, window.showModalDialog
and showModelessDialog, window.close() default action, dialogArguments / returnValue (dialog size and title
from options and the page). The modal loop of a dialog called from a page script lets mshtml's tasks run
(like a synchronous XHR does), otherwise the dialog document never loaded and the call hung. A navigation
with no client site no longer dereferences it. mshta.exe runs RunHTMLApplication.

